// Package rails.v1 is the contract every rail adapter implements:
// swiftbon.paylony.service (NGN, primary), swiftbon.juice.service (NGN payout
// fallback), swiftbon.fcy.service (USD, GBP, EUR) and, later, a partner bank.
// Payouts, onboarding, account and treasury call it without knowing the vendor.
//
// What an adapter is, and is not:
//
//   - It talks to one provider. It owns that provider's credentials, code lists
//     and quirks, and maps them onto the types here.
//   - It has NO ledger effect on payouts. SubmitPayout asks the provider to move
//     money; debiting the customer is postings' job, done by payouts after the
//     adapter reports acceptance. An adapter never calls PostTransaction for a
//     payout.
//   - For inbound money it does call postings (credit and screening hold in one
//     transaction) and publishes inbound-payment-received.
//
// An adapter that does not support an RPC returns gRPC UNIMPLEMENTED (Juice has
// no sub-accounts and no inflows), and Capabilities says so up front so a caller
// does not have to find out by failing.
//
// Errors are gRPC statuses carrying a google.rpc.ErrorInfo with domain
// "rails.swiftbon.com". Branch on the reason, never on the message:
//
//   reason                 grpc code            meaning
//   VALIDATION             INVALID_ARGUMENT     the request is malformed
//   UNSUPPORTED            UNIMPLEMENTED        this adapter does not do that
//   NOT_FOUND              NOT_FOUND            no such sub-account, RFI or payout
//   PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE   UNAVAILABLE          provider down; outcome unknown for writes
//   PROVIDER_REFUSED       FAILED_PRECONDITION  provider refused; see SubmitPayoutResponse
